et servers through heartbeat, recovery (handle the permanent loss of a tablet server) based on WAL (write-ahead log) and metadata, and start/kill the servers. The tablet servers support garbage collection (only keep the last five inserted values), maintaining the memtable for effective searching (memtable would spilled to disk when there are a hundred unique row keys exists), maintaining the in-memory indexes, sharding when a table contains more than 1000 row keys, WAL, reconstructing the tablet server state using WAL and SSTables maintained in the persistent storage, effective range searching in SSTables.","topics":[],"score":259662,"global_rank":50265,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":9300}]